      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cassert>\n\nstruct FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    int idx, size;\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return 0;\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return sign * x;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    std::vector<int> pref((size_t)(n + 1) * n, 0);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        const int base = i * n;\n        const int prev = (i - 1) * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            pref[base + j] = pref[prev + j] + fs.nextInt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    assert(s > 0 && s < n && n < 8000);\n\n    int mxSum = INT_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        const int rowStart = i * n;\n        const int rowEnd   = (i + s) * n;\n        const int* top    = &pref[rowStart];\n        const int* bottom = &pref[rowEnd];\n\n        int window = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n            window += bottom[j] - top[j];\n        }\n        int curMax = window;\n\n        for (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\n            window += (bottom[j] - top[j]) - (bottom[j - s] - top[j - s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n        }\n\n        if (curMax > mxSum) mxSum = curMax;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Fixing the missing cassert include and replacing slow formatted I/O with a custom fread scanner reduces serial overhead, while the existing row-parallel sliding-window algorithm with OpenMP static scheduling and max reduction efficiently uses all cores.",
